  "prefLabel": "He-P 1610.04 Chewable Surfaces",
  "priorExpiration": "2011-09-01",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-P 1610.04 Chewable Surfaces.\n\n(a) When implementing interim controls for lead exposure hazards, an owner shall implement procedures for lead-based paint stabilization in accordance with He-P 1610.02.\n\n(b) When interim controls are implemented for baseboards that meet the definition of a lead exposure hazard, quarter round or similar molding shall be applied to the top to remove the chewable edge.\n\n(c) When interim controls are implemented for interior and exterior windowsills, plastic wallpaper corner guards, or a similar material, shall be securely affixed to the top and bottom of the edge to prevent a child from mouthing the sill.\n\nSource. #5920, eff 1-1-95; ss by #7181, eff 12-24-99; ss by #7495, eff 5-23-01; ss by #8039, eff 2-13-04; ss by #8932, eff 7-6-07; ss by #9986, eff 9-1-11, EXPIRED: 9-1-11 (from He-P 1606.05)\n\nNew. #13052, eff 6-11-20; ss by #14230, eff 4-2-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-p1600.html"
